==Evolution==
Evolves into '''HMS Princess CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''HMS Princess II CC''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Here, Kerihime is as useless as she tends to be. Her Normal and Evolved Forms are pretty much useless due to their low stats. In  regards to her crowd-control capability, HMS Princess CC is good, but getting her at enough levels to deal decent damage is outright impossible, especially because she's a collab unit.

==='''True Form'''===
Compared to Kerihime in her previous forms, her True Form actually can be useful. She has lower than average DPS and range, but since she's cheap and allows you to earn twice the money from enemies defeated, she can be used to level up your wallet quickly while effectively dealing some damage to enemies.

The Premium Ship can now be considered good, and her lower stats are more in line with her lower cost. Good collab units are rarer than you would expect, and although her stats make her feel like a glorified Super Rare, you should feel lucky having her!

==='''Talents'''===
Despite low stats, the Premium Ship has a low cost and recharge, so the stats boosts won't go to waste. Survive also gives her a chance to continue earning money, so that's also worth it.

Kerihime also gets immunities to weaken and wave attacks. Weaken immunity helps to keep her DPS afloat, however there are not many relevant usages, not worth the NP. Wave immunity simply extends her usage to wave enemies, and she outranges almost all of them, but her damage might not falter them.

If there was a reason not to invest, it's that her stats are still low, even if the cost makes up for them. She's also rivaling [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog]] as a budgeted Uber, and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] in terms of being able to make money without losing too much. Luckily, the Premium Ship is good regardless, and she has [[Area Attack]], but it's better to invest in other units. Just remember, it's definitely not a bad idea to invest in her, and she becomes a better [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Miyamoku Musashi]], with more than double the stats and lower cost and recharge.

